I'm guessing here: You try to change the util/lev_lex.c, and changes
to that file are gone during the build?  Note that the pregenerated
lev_lex.c is in sys/share/lev_lex.c, and the Makefile copies it from
sys/share/lev_lex.c to util/lev_lex.c.


> However, the "<MAPC>[-|}{+ABCISHKPLYWTF\\#. 0123456789]*\r?\n {" line
> is not in lev_lex.c, and I don't see any similar lines.  Once again,
> though, I have no idea what the majority of lev_lex does.
> 

Correct, that line wouldn't show up in lev_lex.c; lev_lex.c is
generated by "lex" (or "flex") from util/lev_comp.l

See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lex_(software)


Make sure you have flex and bison installed in such a place that
VC++ can see them.
http://gnuwin32.sourceforge.net/packages/flex.htm
http://gnuwin32.sourceforge.net/packages/bison.htm

Look at the main Makefile where it says
# Yacc/Lex ... if you got 'em.

and a bit further from that, uncomment the lines that say
#DO_YACC  = YACC_ACT
#DO_LEX   = LEX_ACT

and change the lines that define YACC and LEX so they say
YACC   = bison -y
LEX     = flex

And then compiling should create the lev_lex.c from lev_comp.l

